    "turn_text": "Right. And so when you look at some of the things and it says, well, you know, honor your father and mother and don't steal and don't murder people and don't cheat and don't lie and don't worship idols. And people say, well, why? I mean, If you don't trust and you don't lean on the Lord for support and you don't trust in the Lord, then you don't need to follow any of these things or just suggestions, not something to manufacture. And so without that basic lesson, without this following that instruction of trusting in the Lord with all your heart or trusting in the Lord with your feelings, your will and your intellect and leaning on him for your support and making your decisions, then none of the commands or any of the precepts of any religion for that matter or possible. Now, let me just say one more point. This doesn't mean you don't use your own intellect, your own understanding. One of the great things is that in the very beginning, the Lord makes very clear that we are created in His image. And in my mind, when you're created in His image, for example, the Lord is creative. He's a creator. He created the entire universe. And so we are created in His image, that means we are also creative. So when you see expressions of that in art and in literature and in all sorts of things that we do in human endeavors. So it's a reflection of why we're created in the image, but one of the things that we're created in this image, and that includes intellect. So the Lord is the Lord of physics. He's the Lord of science. Science is but a brief, small little glimpse at the much broader and more complex. nature of the creator of the universe. And so it doesn't mean we don't use those things that we've been given by our creator, our intellect and our understanding and to form plans and to pursue them. It just means that as we do so, we are trusting, we are confident, we are unsure that the commands He has given us apply to that. That when after there comes a time when what our will and our intellect put us in conflict with what the Lord has instructed us to do in circumstances such as those, we can either side with and lean on the creator of the universe. So we can decide that we mortals who were fortunate live 90 years, 85 years on this earth somehow have more knowledge than the person who made the whole universe. And that, to me, is sort of a fundamental without that. You're not going to follow this. You might as well not follow any of it because it just won't make any sense to you.",
