  {
    "episode_id": 82325,
    "turn_file": "/shared/3/projects/podcasts/transcriptionQueue/turns/pol_appearance_episodes_interviews/8/2/82325.jsonl",
    "turn_idx": 28,
    "turn_text": "Right. So it came from somewhere, right? Some people, we didn't, there wasn't like this think tank that came up with the stuff. These are the so many of our laws and so many of our policies. So in America, for example, we honor our father and mother, and not legally. You know, there's not a law against disrespecting your parents, but it's the reason why we care about people that are retired. I believe it's the reason why we have Social Security, where we have Medicare, where we have nursing care facilities, why we treat people, why we have hospice care. These are all things that we do as a society that they were pure economic decisions, you know, that they wouldn't make sense from an efficiency standard. That's the way you're judging the world. But if you're judging the world from a moral perspective, that's why we honor our father and mother in these things in these ways. So I think that's really important to remember too.",
    "speaker_id": "SPEAKER_01",
    "inferred_speaker_name": null,
    "inferred_speaker_role": null,
    "chosen_text_key": "transcript",
