    "turn_text": "And sometimes it's just something I read that morning and it spoke to me. So I try to do that regularly. It doesn't take a lot of time, but you sort of go into it. And then Catholicism is very, which I am a Catholic Catholicism is very intellectually deep. So in the Catholic Bible underneath these passages, there's pretty extensive commentary on what it meant. And so that gives you a little bit more depth. We're not talking about an hour. I'm about 15, 20 minutes in the morning before the emails and the phone calls start. I try to do that every day. I don't always do it, but I try to do that every day to the extent I can. And I find that's a pretty good investment time. If you do that every day, that's 365 passages a year. It starts to add up and sort of you start to build context.",
